// Reference recordings (brief B28 Part C). Each file: 16-bit mono PCM WAV at 4 kHz, retrieved 2026-11-21.
// Reproduce a file from its original (downloaded from the primary page named in `source`) with
//   python3 -I docs/research/heart-sound-clips-convert.py ORIGINAL.ogg assets/sounds/reference/<file> START_S END_S
// (needs GStreamer: oggdemux, vorbisdec, audioresample, wavenc). The arguments per file are in the
// `convert:` comment above each entry. The script decodes, downmixes to mono, resamples to 4 kHz,
// cuts (END_S 0 keeps the whole clip), fades 5 ms at both ends and peak-normalises to -6 dBFS.
